# .loom/resync-ignore — paths Loom must not overwrite or delete.
#
# One `.loom/`-relative path per line. Blank lines and `#` comments are
# ignored; matching is exact (no globs). See `.loom/docs/repo-owned-files.md`.
#
# WHY these 5 guard hooks are pinned
# ----------------------------------
# They are a locally-vendored fork. Since Loom was installed here they have
# accumulated ~20 repo-local `fix(guard)` commits (see
# `git log --oneline -- .loom/hooks/`) that were never contributed back to
# Loom's own `defaults/hooks/` baseline. `resync-installed.sh` overwrites
# rather than merges, so every resync silently reverts all of them and breaks
# the `.loom/hooks/tests/*.sh` suites.
#
# This has already happened twice:
#   - `c7ba31d` reverted the PR #19/#20 guard fixes — issue #25, fixed by PR #27.
#   - `2f96421` (2026-08-18 resync) did it again, dropping the same fixes and
#     breaking 8/9 hook test suites; main stayed red for 11 pushes over 3 days
#     — issue #206, restored by PR #208.
#
# Issue #209 added this pin so a third occurrence cannot happen.
#
# SCOPE: this pin stops `./.loom/scripts/resync-installed.sh` (the source of
# both incidents) from overwriting these files, and stops the installer's
# clean sweep from deleting them. It does NOT protect against a full reinstall
# (`install.sh --confirm-reinstall`, `loom update`, `loom-daemon init --force`),
# which re-copies whatever the current `defaults/` tree ships.
#
# Remove an entry ONLY once its local fixes are confirmed upstreamed into
# Loom's own `defaults/hooks/` (github.com/rjwalters/loom).
hooks/guard-background-subagents.sh
hooks/guard-destructive-generic.sh
hooks/guard-destructive.sh
hooks/guard-loom-workflow.sh
hooks/guard-worktree-paths.sh
#
# WHY these 5 hook test suites are pinned (issue #282)
# ---------------------------------------------------
# Upstream's `defaults/hooks/tests/` sources each suite's hook under test from
# `$REPO_ROOT/defaults/hooks/` — the correct layout for the Loom SOURCE repo,
# which ships a defaults/ tree. This consumer repo does not, so those 5 suites
# died at their setup `cp` and silently executed zero assertions (the other 11
# suites already read `$REPO_ROOT/.loom/hooks/`). Issue #282 retargeted them to
# `.loom/hooks/` and added an explicit `[[ ! -d defaults ]]` layout-pinning
# assertion, mirroring the healthy-sibling pattern. Without this pin the next
# `resync-installed.sh` would revert the suites to the defaults/-pathed
# upstream text and they would fail at setup again.
#
# SCOPE: same as the hook pins above — blocks resync overwrite and installer
# deletion; does not survive a full reinstall.
#
# Remove these entries ONLY once rjwalters/loom ships a layout-aware fix
# (defaults/-pathed suites that fall back to `.loom/` in consumer repos) and
# this repo has resynced to it.
hooks/tests/test-guard-background-subagents.sh
hooks/tests/test-guard-loom-workspace.sh
hooks/tests/test-guard-worktree-paths.sh
hooks/tests/test-methodology-inject.sh
hooks/tests/test-skill-router.sh
